  "hints": [
    "Distinct indices do not require distinct values.",
    "Sort, fix two indices, then search the remaining suffix from both ends.",
    "Move left or right according to the four-value sum; skip equal fixed choices and equal endpoints after a match.",
    "Two fixed loops plus a linear two-pointer scan cost O(n^3). Preserve multiplicities and emit each value quadruplet once."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sorting makes the remaining pair sum monotone. Keep first < second < left < right. A small sum needs a larger left value; a large sum needs a smaller right value. On equality record the values and skip repeated choices. Sorting a set would destroy needed occurrences. Python integers safely handle intermediate sums beyond signed 32-bit limits.",
